    </p><a href="/">← Home</a><pagefind-searchbox></pagefind-searchbox><script type="module" src="/pagefind/pagefind-component-ui.js"></script><script type="text/javascript" src="/static/pagefind.js"></script><h1 class="instruction-section" data-pagefind-body="1" data-pagefind-weight="10" data-pagefind-sort="title">WFIT</h1><p class="insn_subtitle" data-pagefind-body="1">Wait for interrupt with timeout</p>
      <p class="aml" data-pagefind-body="1">This instruction provides a hint that the PE
can enter a low-power state and remain there until either a local timeout event
or a wakeup event occurs.
For more information, see <a class="armarm-xref" title="Reference to Armv8 ARM section" data-linkend="BEIJBEJD">Wait For Interrupt</a>.</p>
      <p class="aml" data-pagefind-body="1">As described in <a class="armarm-xref" title="Reference to Armv8 ARM section" data-linkend="BEIJBEJD">Wait For Interrupt</a>, the execution
of a <span class="asm-code">WFIT</span> instruction that would otherwise cause entry to a low-power
state can be trapped to a higher Exception level.</p>
    
